 "title": "Caching",
 "short": "Keep hot answers in fast memory so you don't redo slow work.",
 "what": "A cache is a small, fast store, usually memory, that keeps copies of answers you already worked out. Before doing the slow thing (a database query, an API call), you check the cache. Most apps read the same few things again and again, so most reads become fast.",
 "analogy": "Keys in a bowl by the front door instead of a drawer upstairs. What you use all the time lives close at hand.",
